From ad4d310d927ea62d96f035296acb819860a5b478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:12:38 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] vkr: keep internal queue sync fences non-exportable

The queue sync fences are created, submitted, waited on, reset and
destroyed by the Venus renderer itself and are never exported. Commit
e37c9b0b ("vkr: make internal fences exportable") made them SYNC_FD
exportable for a per-context virgl_renderer_export_fence() that never
uses them.

Exportable fences can be much more expensive to wait on. With the NVIDIA
595.58.03 driver (aarch64), vkWaitForFences() takes about 10.08 ms for an
exportable fence versus 0.10 ms for a plain one, because the driver polls
in 10 ms sleeps. The sync thread waits on one of these fences for every
retired guest fence, so every Venus submission picks up that latency.

Create the fences without VkExportFenceCreateInfo. Guest-created fences,
vkResetFenceResourceMESA and virgl's fence export path are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Ahsan Hussain <ahsan.hussain@siemens.com>
---
 src/venus/vkr_queue.c | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_queue.c b/src/venus/vkr_queue.c
index 61b94bef..24e27755 100644
--- a/src/venus/vkr_queue.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_queue.c
@@ -28,13 +28,13 @@ vkr_device_alloc_queue_sync(struct vkr_device *dev,
       if (!sync)
          return NULL;
 
-      const VkExportFenceCreateInfo export_info = {
-         .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_EXPORT_FENCE_CREATE_INFO,
-         .handleTypes = VK_EXTERNAL_FENCE_HANDLE_TYPE_SYNC_FD_BIT,
-      };
+      /* These fences are only waited on by the sync thread and are never
+       * exported. Keep them non-exportable: some drivers (e.g. NVIDIA)
+       * implement vkWaitForFences on exportable fences as a 10 ms sleep-poll,
+       * which adds up to 10 ms of latency to every retired virtio-gpu fence.
+       */
       const struct VkFenceCreateInfo create_info = {
          .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_FENCE_CREATE_INFO,
-         .pNext = dev->physical_device->KHR_external_fence_fd ? &export_info : NULL,
       };
       VkResult result =
          vk->CreateFence(dev->base.handle.device, &create_info, NULL, &sync->fence);
